Keep niri's DPMS off/on path symmetric, and never remove the output.

An earlier revision ran `niri msg output DP-1 off` before the DPMS-off. That
removes DP-1 from niri's output list, and the only API that brings a removed
output back (`niri msg output DP-1 on`) is a no-op for an output niri no longer
knows about, so the wake path could not restore the display at all.

The DPMS-on side was equally aggressive: it retried `niri msg output DP-1 on`
15 times and then ran `niri msg action quit --skip-confirmation` as a fallback,
which tore down the whole session whenever the retries failed.

Both sides now use niri's built-in power-off-monitors / power-on-monitors only.
This is a comment-only patch against the current Noctalia release.

--- a/Services/Compositor/NiriService.qml
+++ b/Services/Compositor/NiriService.qml
@@ -247,6 +247,11 @@
 
   function turnOffMonitors() {
     try {
+      // Do NOT run `niri msg output DP-1 off` before the DPMS-off. That
+      // removes DP-1 from niri's output list, and the only API that brings a
+      // removed output back (`niri msg output DP-1 on`) is a no-op for an
+      // output niri no longer knows about. The wake path then cannot restore
+      // the display at all.
       Niri.dispatch(["power-off-monitors"]);
     } catch (e) {
       Logger.e("NiriService", "Failed to turn off monitors:", e);
@@ -255,6 +260,12 @@
 
   function turnOnMonitors() {
     try {
+      // Keep the DPMS-on path symmetric with turnOffMonitors(). An earlier
+      // revision retried `niri msg output DP-1 on` 15x and then ran
+      // `niri msg action quit --skip-confirmation` as a fallback, which tore
+      // down the whole session whenever the retries failed. niri's built-in
+      // DPMS-on is sufficient now that the flapping connector is handled by
+      // the xHCI/USB-hub udev rules in hosts/faex1/default.nix.
       Niri.dispatch(["power-on-monitors"]);
     } catch (e) {
       Logger.e("NiriService", "Failed to turn on monitors:", e);
